WEBVTT

02:11.770 --> 02:14.610
<b>Unified Year 1927, May 26th, Imperial Capital Berun Central Station</b>

02:14.690 --> 02:19.910
<b>This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.</b>

02:23.320 --> 02:26.260
<b>Is ours the type of relationship 
where you have to see me off?</b>

02:26.260 --> 02:29.440
<b>I almost never get to see you 
in an embarrassing position.</b>

02:29.440 --> 02:31.850
<b>I refuse to miss the opportunity.</b>

02:36.210 --> 02:40.220
<b>Episode Five
Unlucky Draw</b>

02:36.770 --> 02:39.450
<b>You had an unlucky draw, huh?</b>

02:40.440 --> 02:42.230
<b>There's no helping it.</b>

02:42.230 --> 02:45.530
<b>I was the one who went against
high leadership.</b>

02:46.400 --> 02:48.330
<b>The government itself may fall.</b>

02:49.080 --> 02:51.980
<b>...the Imperial Family 
itself may be in danger.</b>

02:52.180 --> 02:55.340
<b>I expected to be relieved of my position
as Deputy Chief of War Affairs, but...</b>

02:55.790 --> 02:58.530
<b>I'm surprised to see 
I'm only being transferred.</b>

02:59.700 --> 03:01.990
<b>I'm not being sent anywhere.</b>

03:03.520 --> 03:06.690
<b>Even though we both went 
against leadership.</b>

03:06.690 --> 03:08.530
<b>It's not fair at all.</b>

03:08.530 --> 03:10.640
<b>We're soldiers.</b>

03:10.640 --> 03:13.090
<b>We have no choice but to obey 
the will of the nation.</b>

03:13.840 --> 03:17.330
<b>There's no one else in Strategic HQ</b>

03:19.030 --> 03:23.480
<b>with your political skills or 
understanding of the operation.</b>

03:25.480 --> 03:27.880
<b>And you'll have no one to complain to.</b>

03:28.840 --> 03:30.230
<b>That's right.</b>

03:30.230 --> 03:33.140
<b>I really don't think 
we can do without you...</b>

03:34.330 --> 03:35.760
<b>It seems it's time.</b>

03:39.780 --> 03:41.660
<b>I'll leave the East to you.</b>

03:41.960 --> 03:45.280
<b>We'll win this war together.</b>

03:45.280 --> 03:47.780
<b>Yeah, that's right.</b>

03:48.160 --> 03:49.700
<b>I'll pray for your good luck.</b>

03:49.700 --> 03:52.410
<b>Come back as a victorious general.</b>

03:52.410 --> 03:55.590
<b>Get the expensive booze and cigars ready.</b>

03:55.590 --> 03:57.330
<b>I'll drive you bankrupt.</b>

04:07.870 --> 04:10.230
<b>Win the war together, huh?</b>

04:11.960 --> 04:16.270
<b>Even a single failure will 
put the Empire in danger.</b>

04:16.930 --> 04:21.170
<b>No matter how many times the Federation 
fails, it will keep coming back.</b>

04:26.030 --> 04:28.870
<b>It's not fair at all.</b>

04:33.360 --> 04:38.370
<b><i>A military officer can be sent 
anywhere alone with a single order.</i></b>

04:38.370 --> 04:41.700
<b><i>But my influence in the East is limited.</i></b>

04:41.700 --> 04:44.390
<b><i>I have no pieces to play 
at all, realistically.</i></b>

04:45.940 --> 04:49.270
<b>No, I do have one.</b>

04:49.300 --> 04:51.350
<b>Eastern Battlefront Imperial Eastern Theater Frontline Base</b>

04:54.960 --> 05:00.110
<b><i>Why? Why am I being summoned 
by Eastern Theater Command?</i></b>

05:00.110 --> 05:02.200
<b><i>Something to do with the peace talks?</i></b>

05:02.200 --> 05:05.360
<b><i>But then why aren't we being 
given a ceasefire order?</i></b>

05:05.360 --> 05:10.790
<b><i>The Ildoa observer said that a ceasefire 
was just a matter of time...</i></b>

05:12.440 --> 05:17.060
<b><i>Well, there's no way we can 
continue the war, regardless.</i></b>

05:17.510 --> 05:21.510
<b><i>Anybody capable of making logical 
decisions would know that.</i></b>

05:22.240 --> 05:25.060
<b><i>The brass can't possibly be that stu...</i></b>

05:25.790 --> 05:26.850
<b>huh?</b>

05:28.340 --> 05:32.350
<b>It's been a long time, 
Lt. Colonel Degurechaff.</b>

05:39.550 --> 05:43.820
<b>S-Sir, what are you doing here?</b>

05:44.230 --> 05:47.130
<b>Strategic HQ has sent me into exile.</b>

05:47.130 --> 05:49.410
<b>I'll be here from now on.</b>

05:49.660 --> 05:54.540
<b><i>E-Exiled? The boss of my 
faction has screwed up?!</i></b>

05:55.690 --> 05:57.620
<b>Is something wrong?</b>

05:57.620 --> 06:00.790
<b>Sorry! I was just dizzy 
from lack of sleep...</b>

06:00.790 --> 06:02.880
<b><i>Shit! Shit! Shit!</i></b>

06:02.880 --> 06:05.710
<b><i>My whole career plan is in danger!</i></b>

06:05.710 --> 06:09.740
<b><i>I was counting on my faction's boss to 
write me a letter of recommendation!</i></b>

06:09.740 --> 06:14.390
<b><i>No, wait. If there's a peace treaty, 
maybe I won't need it...</i></b>

06:14.720 --> 06:15.480
<b>By the way...</b>

06:15.480 --> 06:17.470
<b>Peace negotiations have 
broken down, you see.</b>

06:18.960 --> 06:24.730
<b>High leadership wants more victories to 
ensure better conditions in the deal.</b>

06:24.730 --> 06:28.600
<b>I was opposed to this, so they 
got angry and sent me here.</b>

06:28.600 --> 06:31.700
<b><i>Wh-What?!</i></b>

06:31.700 --> 06:35.340
<b><i>The peace negotiations broke down, 
and the leadership hates my boss!</i></b>

06:35.340 --> 06:36.880
<b><i>This is as bad as it could possibly get!</i></b>

06:37.230 --> 06:38.930
<b>Hey. Hey.</b>

06:38.930 --> 06:39.870
<b>Are you okay?</b>

06:40.260 --> 06:44.030
<b>Sorry! I got a little dizzy from shock...</b>

06:44.940 --> 06:46.600
<b>That won't do.</b>

06:46.600 --> 06:50.550
<b>I'm going to need you to work 
even harder than before.</b>

06:50.550 --> 06:54.310
<b><i>They're still going to 
overwork me, even now?</i></b>

06:54.310 --> 06:57.710
<b>Now, due to the political 
circumstances I just described,</b>

06:57.710 --> 07:02.290
<b>I'll be working on a large-scale 
offensive in the East.</b>

07:02.970 --> 07:05.280
<b>The Andromeda Project?</b>

07:05.690 --> 07:09.760
<b>The main goal of the operation is to 
ensure better conditions in a peace deal.</b>

07:10.230 --> 07:13.940
<b>And that means crushing 
the enemy's will to resist.</b>

07:14.630 --> 07:16.790
<b>Specifically, we've 
decided to take control</b>

07:16.790 --> 07:19.790
<b>of the Federation army's 
resource-producing areas.</b>

07:20.170 --> 07:24.720
<b>We'll be splitting the Eastern army into 
A Group, which will handle the offensive,</b>

07:24.720 --> 07:28.550
<b>and B Group, which will 
maintain the battle lines.</b>

07:28.550 --> 07:32.290
<b>A strikes. B defends.</b>

07:32.290 --> 07:35.050
<b>If this operation works,</b>

07:35.050 --> 07:39.700
<b>it will maintain our forces' ability 
to fight while weakening the enemy's.</b>

07:39.700 --> 07:43.250
<b>It should help us in negotiations.</b>

07:43.250 --> 07:46.250
<b>And General Zettour has headed to the East</b>

07:46.250 --> 07:49.820
<b>to observe and take command of B Group.</b>

07:49.820 --> 07:52.210
<b>It's de facto exile, actually.</b>

07:52.210 --> 07:56.770
<b>The high leadership doesn't 
like being talked down.</b>

07:57.620 --> 08:00.400
<b>I understand the operation.</b>

08:00.400 --> 08:03.710
<b>But negotiations in Ildoa...</b>

08:05.140 --> 08:08.600
<b>Are to be temporarily stopped, I'm told.</b>

08:09.860 --> 08:13.320
<b>If leadership wants a win, 
then we have to win.</b>

08:13.710 --> 08:15.510
<b>No matter what.</b>

08:16.710 --> 08:18.640
<b>I'll ask for your honest opinion.</b>

08:18.640 --> 08:21.860
<b>What do you think of 
the Andromeda Project?</b>

08:22.830 --> 08:27.350
<b>Honestly, it's nothing short of reckless.</b>

08:28.220 --> 08:30.100
<b>Continue.</b>

08:30.380 --> 08:34.560
<b>B Group's assigned territory 
is already far too large.</b>

08:34.560 --> 08:36.620
<b>They don't have the men for it.</b>

08:36.620 --> 08:39.980
<b>And if A Group's offensive succeeds,</b>

08:39.980 --> 08:43.180
<b>it will only mean more territory 
for them to defend.</b>

08:43.180 --> 08:46.250
<b>B Group is a rubber band, 
stretched to its breaking point.</b>

08:46.870 --> 08:48.620
<b>You don't need scissors to snap it.</b>

08:48.620 --> 08:50.950
<b>A single poke from a needle could do it.</b>

08:51.300 --> 08:55.640
<b>And if I may, I dislike 
the project's name.</b>

08:55.980 --> 08:57.710
<b>The project's name?</b>

08:58.170 --> 09:03.220
<b>The name suggests a distant horizon, 
or the stars in outer space.</b>

09:03.220 --> 09:07.030
<b>It's romantic, in a way, but I 
find it far too distant a goal.</b>

09:08.360 --> 09:10.100
<b>An excellent point!</b>

09:10.100 --> 09:14.780
<b>The one who named it may look rough, 
but they're surprisingly delicate.</b>

09:16.880 --> 09:20.170
<b>Your points are all logical.</b>

09:20.170 --> 09:23.910
<b>But unfortunately, we aren't 
allowed to make any changes.</b>

09:23.910 --> 09:27.410
<b>Come up with a defense plan for B Group.</b>

09:27.410 --> 09:29.710
<b>A plan?</b>

09:30.190 --> 09:32.910
<b>What do we need for a successful defense?</b>

09:33.670 --> 09:38.680
<b>The initiative. Without the 
initiative, we have nothing.</b>

09:38.680 --> 09:40.610
<b>An unchanging fact of warfare.</b>

09:40.610 --> 09:42.940
<b>The question is, how do we get it?</b>

09:42.940 --> 09:46.170
<b>It's hard to say since 
we're on the inferior side...</b>

09:46.520 --> 09:48.520
<b>Let's aim for a counterattack.</b>

09:48.520 --> 09:50.740
<b>We'll lure the enemy in with a decoy</b>

09:50.740 --> 09:52.940
<b>and wipe them out when 
they're overextended.</b>

09:53.410 --> 09:55.110
<b>Easier said than done.</b>

09:55.110 --> 09:58.930
<b>Yes. We need something they'll feel 
is worth taking the chance on.</b>

09:58.930 --> 10:02.810
<b>And the decoy will have to have 
the tenacity to stay in the fight</b>

10:02.810 --> 10:04.610
<b>until the fish has swallowed the lure.</b>

10:04.910 --> 10:07.290
<b>That, I don't think we 
need to worry about.</b>

10:07.290 --> 10:10.380
<b>I have a card I can play.</b>

10:10.700 --> 10:14.710
<b><i>I don't know who he's referring to, 
but I feel bad for them.</i></b>

10:15.280 --> 10:20.630
<b>We'll also need hunters who can destroy 
the enemy once they've engaged the decoy.</b>

10:20.630 --> 10:25.120
<b>Hmm... what spare forces 
do we have in the East?</b>

10:25.120 --> 10:28.890
<b>B Group does have 
a mechanized division...</b>

10:28.890 --> 10:31.480
<b>But we can't let them go easily.</b>

10:31.480 --> 10:36.260
<b>Which means our only easily available 
forces are your combat team.</b>

10:37.510 --> 10:42.370
<b>Oh, don't worry. I'm a hard man to 
work for, but I won't ask for that.</b>

10:42.370 --> 10:44.500
<b>I appreciate your concern, sir!</b>

10:44.500 --> 10:47.240
<b>Oh, no need to thank me.</b>

10:47.560 --> 10:51.480
<b>You're going to be the bait, after all.</b>

10:51.480 --> 10:56.670
<b>Even I can't ask you to be both 
the bait and the hunter.</b>

10:56.670 --> 11:02.670
<b>Um... I'm... the bait?</b>

11:02.670 --> 11:04.400
<b>This was your idea.</b>

11:04.400 --> 11:07.350
<b>Of course I'll ask you to 
be the one to carry it out.</b>

11:08.030 --> 11:10.990
<b>The bait is the group that put 
their capital city to the torch.</b>

11:10.990 --> 11:13.780
<b>I've little doubt they'll bite.</b>

11:19.620 --> 11:22.790
<b>But I suppose we don't 
have enough forces?</b>

11:22.790 --> 11:26.120
<b>Even if we did use that 
mechanized division...</b>

11:26.120 --> 11:28.120
<b>That's correct!</b>

11:28.120 --> 11:29.880
<b>While I do hate to say it,</b>

11:29.880 --> 11:33.360
<b>it seems my idea has 
little chance of working,</b>

11:33.360 --> 11:35.440
<b>so I'll come up with another one!</b>

11:35.440 --> 11:36.040
<b>Bye!</b>

11:36.810 --> 11:39.750
<b>I'll use one of your companies!</b>

11:43.270 --> 11:45.130
<b>Did you not hear me?</b>

11:45.130 --> 11:47.590
<b>Give me one of your mage companies.</b>

11:47.590 --> 11:48.980
<b>That'll be enough.</b>

11:48.980 --> 11:51.110
<b>We're splitting our forces?</b>

11:51.110 --> 11:52.050
<b>Indeed.</b>

11:52.050 --> 11:56.740
<b>I-If I may, sir, my companies 
aren't just normal companies!</b>

11:56.740 --> 12:00.870
<b>And if we're going to be on defense, 
we need mages to have any chance!</b>

12:00.870 --> 12:03.250
<b>It'll be like having 
our limbs ripped off.</b>

12:03.250 --> 12:05.990
<b>Don't worry. Lots of 
people have lost a limb.</b>

12:05.990 --> 12:10.230
<b>Y-You insist on taking 
one of my companies?</b>

12:10.230 --> 12:14.040
<b>Otherwise, I won't be able to 
save you when you're surrounded.</b>

12:20.300 --> 12:24.630
<b>If you'll take Grantz, one of my 
young lieutenants, and his unit...</b>

12:25.200 --> 12:26.570
<b>Thank you.</b>

12:26.570 --> 12:28.140
<b>Now, as for the specifics...</b>

12:29.000 --> 12:31.630
<b>Look. This is the spot.</b>

12:31.940 --> 12:34.780
<b>Soldim 528?</b>

12:34.780 --> 12:38.570
<b>It was originally a 
Federation rail depot.</b>

12:38.570 --> 12:42.490
<b>The Empire occupied it during Iron Hammer,</b>

12:42.490 --> 12:45.780
<b>but the units stationed there were pulled,
and it's essentially abandoned.</b>

12:46.300 --> 12:50.510
<b>It's located along rail routes 
and can serve as a supply depot.</b>

12:50.510 --> 12:54.550
<b>The enemy would love to recapture it.</b>

12:54.870 --> 12:58.760
<b>You're going to be there to welcome them.</b>

12:58.760 --> 13:01.880
<b>You must defend the location at 
all costs until your allies arrive.</b>

13:01.880 --> 13:06.170
<b>Wait! I need permission 
to retreat if I feel...</b>

13:06.170 --> 13:07.130
<b>Impossible.</b>

13:07.850 --> 13:09.220
<b>Defend it at all costs.</b>

13:17.310 --> 13:24.820
<b>Allied Kingdom Military Intelligence Colonel
Sir Isaac Dustin Drake</b>

13:17.700 --> 13:20.340
<b>It's been a long time, Uncle.</b>

13:21.030 --> 13:22.850
<b>William.</b>

13:22.850 --> 13:24.830
<b>As always, you seem upset.</b>

13:24.830 --> 13:29.490
<b>Yes. Our unit's problem child 
has made a friend, you see.</b>

13:30.510 --> 13:35.890
<b>I would appreciate it if Major General 
Habergram would take them off our hands.</b>

13:37.960 --> 13:40.120
<b>I brought you a little gift, at least.</b>

13:40.120 --> 13:43.110
<b>I smuggled it in past Federation customs.</b>

13:43.110 --> 13:45.100
<b>Scotch from home.</b>

13:45.100 --> 13:46.790
<b>How kind of you...</b>

13:50.050 --> 13:52.000
<b>Burn it once you've read it.</b>

13:52.000 --> 13:54.290
<b>It's the latest information from Ultra.</b>

13:54.630 --> 13:55.930
<b>Ultra...</b>

13:56.330 --> 13:59.960
<b>That spy of ours high up in the Empire?</b>

14:00.600 --> 14:02.320
<b>Can they be trusted?</b>

14:02.320 --> 14:04.720
<b>You've heard what the 
Empire's up to, right?</b>

14:04.720 --> 14:08.010
<b>Yes. Codename "Andromeda"?</b>

14:08.010 --> 14:10.050
<b>We've been told to join the fight.</b>

14:10.500 --> 14:13.460
<b>Ultra says that conflict 
between the Empire's military</b>

14:13.460 --> 14:15.840
<b>and civilian leadership is 
what's driving Andromeda.</b>

14:15.840 --> 14:18.220
<b>Well, that's good news.</b>

14:18.220 --> 14:20.450
<b>But even knowing that...</b>

14:20.450 --> 14:22.610
<b>The fight ended with an officer</b>

14:22.610 --> 14:26.450
<b>from their strategic HQ being 
sent to the eastern theater.</b>

14:28.240 --> 14:31.310
<b>Lieutenant General Hans von Zettour.</b>

14:31.310 --> 14:32.960
<b>A hard man to deal with.</b>

14:32.960 --> 14:34.340
<b>How so?</b>

14:34.340 --> 14:35.850
<b>Is he talented?</b>

14:35.850 --> 14:38.610
<b>He is. Terrifyingly so.</b>

14:38.610 --> 14:41.480
<b>If you happen to see him 
on the battlefield...</b>

14:41.820 --> 14:44.830
<b>Kill him. At all costs.</b>

14:54.770 --> 14:58.590
<b>We'd been assuming that 
Federation air power</b>

14:58.590 --> 15:00.830
<b>was destroyed during Iron Hammer...</b>

15:01.320 --> 15:04.920
<b>But the Unified States have 
supplied them with a new air force.</b>

15:04.920 --> 15:09.200
<b>Andromeda's falling apart already, huh?</b>

15:09.740 --> 15:12.500
<b>I'm sure he's not getting 
a moment of sleep.</b>

15:15.570 --> 15:17.110
<b>What's going on?</b>

15:17.110 --> 15:19.850
<b>Why haven't we finalized 
things with Foreign Affairs?</b>

15:19.850 --> 15:25.190
<b>G-General Zettour was unofficially acting 
as a bridge with civilian leadership...</b>

15:25.190 --> 15:26.780
<b>But now...</b>

15:28.150 --> 15:31.660
<b>So what happened to that 
fleet of unknown ships?</b>

15:31.660 --> 15:35.650
<b>The north seas fleet says that 
more and more are coming...</b>

15:35.650 --> 15:36.660
<b><i>Shit.</i></b>

15:36.660 --> 15:40.420
<b><i>We can't have our subs 
just sink them all?</i></b>

15:40.420 --> 15:46.130
<b><i>Our legal experts say it would 
likely violate international law...</i></b>

15:46.130 --> 15:48.040
<b>I needed to know this sooner!</b>

15:54.520 --> 15:56.090
<b>It's Lieutenant Colonel Uger.</b>

15:58.760 --> 16:02.770
<b>Imperial Strategic HQ Railway Command
Maximilian Johann von Uger</b>

15:59.780 --> 16:02.770
<b>The Allied Kingdom did 
another night bombing raid</b>

16:02.770 --> 16:06.340
<b>on our industrial areas to the west.</b>

16:06.340 --> 16:08.860
<b>We're putting together a damage report...</b>

16:08.860 --> 16:12.110
<b>But we don't have enough 
planes to stop them all.</b>

16:12.110 --> 16:14.920
<b>Our industrial productivity 
is falling as a result.</b>

16:14.920 --> 16:17.460
<b>We're already seeing problems 
supplying the Andromeda Project...</b>

16:16.260 --> 16:18.510
<b>Why are you so damn serious?</b>

16:20.570 --> 16:23.890
<b>All you do is read me those damn reports.</b>

16:23.890 --> 16:26.320
<b>You can't even tell me a single joke?</b>

16:28.020 --> 16:29.850
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

16:31.030 --> 16:34.210
<b>Is this... Is this true?</b>

16:34.210 --> 16:36.420
<b>Yes, Comrade Loria.</b>

16:36.420 --> 16:40.720
<b>The Devil of the Rhine is 
commanding the area in question.</b>

16:40.720 --> 16:43.850
<b>The little slut!</b>

16:43.850 --> 16:47.570
<b>Is she tempting me?</b>

16:47.570 --> 16:49.740
<b>Yes, they're a ridiculous bunch.</b>

16:49.740 --> 16:52.430
<b>We should contact the army 
and have them deal with it.</b>

16:52.430 --> 16:55.610
<b>Contact them? Have them deal with it?</b>

16:56.750 --> 16:58.250
<b>Don't be stupid!</b>

16:58.250 --> 16:59.900
<b>We'll take her alive ourselves!</b>

16:59.900 --> 17:02.040
<b>Take her alive?</b>

17:02.040 --> 17:04.780
<b>If she dies in battle, 
she becomes a hero!</b>

17:04.780 --> 17:07.870
<b>She needs to be made an 
example of at a trial!</b>

17:07.870 --> 17:10.010
<b>Don't let her get away! Don't kill her!</b>

17:10.010 --> 17:12.010
<b>Get her alive!</b>

17:17.260 --> 17:19.260
<b>Eastern Theater Soldim 528</b>

17:25.530 --> 17:29.670
<b>We expected to be surrounded, 
but I didn't expect this many men.</b>

17:30.100 --> 17:33.520
<b>I guess we should've expected this 
after what we did to Moskva.</b>

17:33.520 --> 17:36.520
<b>Damn it. I'm jealous of Lt. Grantz.</b>

17:36.520 --> 17:40.030
<b>I hope he doesn't screw something up 
when he's working with the general.</b>

17:40.030 --> 17:44.000
<b>Quite possibly. If we're lucky, 
it just ends with him being fired.</b>

17:44.000 --> 17:46.200
<b>Something worse might happen?!</b>

17:48.470 --> 17:51.830
<b><i>Reinforcements are coming, right?</i></b>

17:52.340 --> 17:54.590
<b>Eastern Battlefront Imperial Eastern Theater Forward Base Strategy Room</b>

17:52.920 --> 17:54.610
<b>Message from Rerugen Combat Team!</b>

17:54.610 --> 17:58.980
<b>Soldim 528 has been surrounded 
by multiple Federation units!</b>

17:59.220 --> 18:00.370
<b>What?</b>

18:00.370 --> 18:03.100
<b>That's not the enemy advance 
route we expected!</b>

18:03.100 --> 18:05.230
<b>What were our scouts and 
observation lines doing?</b>

18:10.040 --> 18:11.390
<b>There's too many of them!</b>

18:11.390 --> 18:13.740
<b>We're outnumbered! They'll swarm us!</b>

18:13.740 --> 18:16.350
<b>Our first defense lines 
are about to be overrun!</b>

18:16.350 --> 18:19.280
<b>They're that deep already?! 
It's too soon!</b>

18:19.280 --> 18:21.690
<b>Hold fast! Buy as much time as we can!</b>

18:22.070 --> 18:23.210
<b><i>This is bad.</i></b>

18:23.210 --> 18:25.970
<b><i>They're getting into 
the city far too fast.</i></b>

18:26.420 --> 18:27.960
<b>All units, situation report!</b>

18:27.960 --> 18:30.750
<b>We've pulled back and 
concealed our armor!</b>

18:30.750 --> 18:32.490
<b>No damage!</b>

18:32.490 --> 18:34.230
<b>Same for our artillery!</b>

18:34.230 --> 18:37.630
<b>We're conserving it, except for those 
units who went to assist the infantry.</b>

18:37.630 --> 18:41.430
<b>I never thought I'd hear 
those words from you.</b>

18:41.430 --> 18:44.520
<b>Lieutenant Colonel!
Lieutenant Tospan has a suggestion!</b>

18:44.520 --> 18:47.020
<b>What? Lieutenant Tospan?</b>

18:47.020 --> 18:50.390
<b>He's not going to do something 
stupid again, is he?</b>

18:50.770 --> 18:52.380
<b>This is Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff!</b>

18:52.380 --> 18:53.150
<b><i>Ma'am!</i></b>

18:53.360 --> 18:56.090
<b>I want to receive an 
order from you, ma'am!</b>

18:56.090 --> 18:58.650
<b><i>I gave you your orders already.</i></b>

18:58.650 --> 19:01.990
<b>Yes. But military doctrine tells us</b>

19:01.990 --> 19:05.670
<b>that we should withdraw in 
the face of a force this size.</b>

19:05.670 --> 19:08.160
<b><i>So I hoped you could use your authority</i></b>

19:08.160 --> 19:10.700
<b><i>as commanding officer to 
tell us to hold the position!</i></b>

19:11.460 --> 19:13.490
<b>Good, good.</b>

19:13.800 --> 19:15.580
<b>I like you, Lieutenant!</b>

19:15.580 --> 19:17.890
<b>I'll send a written order to 
defend the position immediately!</b>

19:17.890 --> 19:19.960
<b>Yes, understood!</b>

19:22.350 --> 19:24.310
<b><i>What's wrong, Lieutenant Tospan?</i></b>

19:24.800 --> 19:30.220
<b>Their heavy artillery! They're 
firing it on top of their own men!</b>

19:30.820 --> 19:32.980
<b>That's disgusting.</b>

19:32.980 --> 19:35.310
<b>They see their own infantry 
as expendable pawns?</b>

19:35.310 --> 19:36.240
<b><i>Lieutenant Colonel!</i></b>

19:36.680 --> 19:38.630
<b>We are prepared to fire back!</b>

19:38.630 --> 19:40.800
<b>No. We'll stop them with our mages.</b>

19:41.280 --> 19:44.220
<b>Major Weiss, knock out 
the enemy's artillery shells!</b>

19:44.220 --> 19:46.590
<b>Are you serious, Lieutenant Colonel?</b>

19:46.590 --> 19:50.950
<b><i>I believe I had you trained on it 
when we formed the battalion.</i></b>

19:51.520 --> 19:55.500
<b>We don't have enough men. Two companies 
can't cover the whole area.</b>

19:55.500 --> 20:00.250
<b>Major Weiss, you're the oldest one here. 
I can't have you acting like that.</b>

20:00.250 --> 20:02.670
<b><i>Or do you need to be re-educated?</i></b>

20:07.090 --> 20:09.230
<b>No, not at all!</b>

20:09.230 --> 20:10.900
<b>Companies 2 and 3!</b>

20:10.900 --> 20:13.400
<b>We'll shoot down the artillery shells 
and knock out their artillery!</b>

20:13.400 --> 20:14.730
<b>Follow me!</b>

20:14.770 --> 20:17.480
<b>Federation Offensive Command Post</b>

20:20.130 --> 20:23.220
<b>May I ask you to take the lead?</b>

20:28.460 --> 20:30.490
<b>Federation mages?</b>

20:30.490 --> 20:33.370
<b>Are those the volunteers 
we fought at Tiegenhoff?!</b>

20:33.370 --> 20:36.200
<b>Stand fast! Prepare penetrator spells!</b>

20:43.840 --> 20:45.460
<b>02! Situation report!</b>

20:45.740 --> 20:48.350
<b><i>02! Situation report! What are you doing?</i></b>

21:08.070 --> 21:10.870
<b><i>Weiss! What's wrong? Weiss!</i></b>

22:43.560 --> 22:45.410
<b>Goodnight.</b>

22:50.510 --> 22:52.160
<b>Lieutenant Colonel Uger?</b>

22:52.740 --> 22:55.130
<b>Oh, Colonel Rerugen.</b>

22:55.130 --> 22:58.230
<b>It's been a while since 
we've met in person.</b>

22:58.230 --> 22:59.820
<b>Have you lost weight?</b>

22:59.820 --> 23:00.930
<b>Yes.</b>

23:00.930 --> 23:03.060
<b>As have you...</b>

23:03.060 --> 23:05.850
<b>We both have difficult jobs.</b>

23:05.850 --> 23:07.690
<b>Why don't we get a drink?</b>

23:07.690 --> 23:09.890
<b>Unfortunately, I still have work...</b>

23:09.890 --> 23:12.190
<b><i>Why are you so damn serious?</i></b>

23:13.680 --> 23:15.240
<b>Colonel Rerugen!</b>

23:21.360 --> 23:23.050
<b>Lieutenant Colonel Uger...</b>

23:23.760 --> 23:27.620
<b>I didn't take you for the type.</b>

23:27.620 --> 23:32.010
<b>For someone with a wife and kids, 
and a position of responsibility,</b>

23:32.010 --> 23:34.730
<b>to say something like that here without 
knowing who else could be around.</b>

23:36.010 --> 23:40.090
<b>Next Time
Decoy</b>
